scripts/paint/paint.mjs generates src/styles/paint.css, the brush-paint textures of the general version (data pages
only): six brush stroke tiles (red, blue and yellow, horizontal and vertical) and the frayed outline used with
-webkit-mask-box-image. It is a line-for-line port of the owner-approved v5 prototype's paint-tex.py (notes:
owner-assets/data-redesign/v5/), including Python's seeded random for the outline, so the output equals the
prototype's. The tiles' source is that SVG noise, but browsers would rasterise it on the main thread on every page, so
the script renders each tile once in headless Chromium, flattens it onto its pigment and commits it as WebP at 1× and
2× (src/styles/paint/; the build hashes them into /_astro/). Run `node scripts/paint/paint.mjs --write` after changing
a pigment (its base must match --ed-red, --ed-blue or --ed-yellow in tokens.css) to rewrite paint.css and the tiles,
`--check` to compare the committed CSS and tiles with a fresh render, `--lab <file>` for a swatch sheet. Rendering
needs Chromium (Playwright's, or CHROME_PATH / PW_CHANNEL). tests/unit/paint.test.ts checks the file, the pigments,
the tiles and the contrast of text on the paint, from the formula and from the tiles' pixels.
